# UX Standards

Hork is a Slack-baseline utility chat: snappy, device-appropriate, lovable
because it works. Full rationale in [`docs/ux.md`](../../docs/ux.md).

## Color roles (never mix)

- **Purple = brand/neutral foundation** — the `gray` scale is purple-tinted;
  `brand.*` for identity moments and selected nav (`nav.selected`)
- **Teal = action** — `action.*` / `preset="primary"` for buttons, links,
  switches, focus rings. Only on things the user can do
- **Status stays semantic** — green success, red error/destructive, amber
  warning, blue info. Never use purple/teal for status, or status hues for chrome
- Use semantic tokens (`surface.canvas|raised|sunken`, `border.subtle`,
  `text.muted`) — not raw hex or component-local colors

## Layout contract

- App frame is fixed-viewport (`AppLayout` in `src/components/AppShell.tsx`):
  desktop (md+) = persistent sidebar (brand + plus at top; user + appearance
  in the footer); mobile
  = compact header, group pages render their own single top bar. Document
  does not scroll — pages scroll internally (`flex={1} minH={0} overflowY="auto"`)
- Chat: chronological messages, composer pinned to bottom, Enter sends
  (Shift+Enter newline), optimistic pending bubbles
- Overlays use `QuickModal` (modal on md+, drawer on mobile; drag-to-dismiss)

## Native / PWA

- **Viewport:** `#root` is `position: fixed`; shell height from
  `visualViewport` (`--app-height`, `--app-offset-top`); fallback `100dvh`.
  Composer stays above the keyboard; focus scrolls inside the nearest
  overflow scrollport only (never the document)
- **Edges:** paint `html`/`body`/`#root` with `surface.canvas`; pad chrome with
  `env(safe-area-inset-*)` (no body+shell double-subtract). `theme-color` +
  manifest colors track canvas (incl. in-app color-mode sync);
  `apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style` = `black-translucent` when edge-to-edge
- **Overlays:** every sheet/dialog has X and/or Cancel; confirmations use the
  same mobile drawer shell as `QuickModal`
- **Menus:** mobile short actions → floating bottom/top action sheet
  (inset, rounded); mobile nav lists (groups) → floating drawer — not `Menu`
  popovers. Desktop may keep `Menu`

## States — never blank

- No `if (error) return null` — use `UI.ErrorState` (with retry) or a toast
- No empty `return null` for lists — use `UI.EmptyState` with a CTA
- Loading: `Skeleton` matching final layout, not bare full-screen spinners
- Submits: button `isLoading` + double-submit guard; failed sends restore input

## Product rules

- Group lists are **membership-scoped** (`useGroups({ userId })`) — never list
  all groups
- Joining is **explicit consent** (join prompt), never a silent side effect
- Ask for a display name right after first sign-in; `···1234` is a fallback,
  not an identity
- Destructive actions (leave/delete/remove) go through `useConfirmation` with
  `isDestructive: true`; never confirm create/send

## Motion budget

2–3 intentional micro-motions only (message appear ~160ms, pressed-state
translate, Chakra modal/drawer defaults). Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
No decorative animation, gradients, or gloss.

## Copy

- User-facing strings say **Hork**, never Quacker; no developer copy in error
  screens (no "Vite", "dev server")
- Errors are human + actionable ("Check your connection and try again.")
